Subject: [PATCH] ios-m0: gate macOS sandbox and libedit dependency

The iOS cross build uses CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Darwin, so CMake's APPLE branch is
true. Several helper services select the macOS Seatbelt sandbox from that branch,
but fakesigned iOS helper processes cannot use Seatbelt and should fall back to
the unimplemented sandbox.

The standalone JS REPL utility is not built for the M0 headless/app targets, so
avoid requiring libedit on iOS as well.
--- a/Meta/CMake/check_for_dependencies.cmake
+++ b/Meta/CMake/check_for_dependencies.cmake
@@ -5 +5 @@
-if (NOT WIN32 AND NOT ANDROID)
+if (NOT WIN32 AND NOT ANDROID AND NOT IOS)
--- a/Services/ImageDecoder/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Services/ImageDecoder/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -27 +27 @@ if (LINUX)
-elseif (APPLE)
+elseif (APPLE AND NOT IOS)
--- a/Services/RequestServer/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Services/RequestServer/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -13 +13 @@ if (LINUX)
-elseif (APPLE)
+elseif (APPLE AND NOT IOS)
--- a/Services/WebContent/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Services/WebContent/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -43 +43 @@ if (LINUX)
-elseif (APPLE)
+elseif (APPLE AND NOT IOS)
--- a/Services/WebWorker/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Services/WebWorker/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -23 +23 @@ if (LINUX)
-elseif (APPLE)
+elseif (APPLE AND NOT IOS)
